{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ContiguousArray\/reserveCapacity(_:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCapacity","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"minimumCapacity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The requested number of elements to store."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are adding a known number of elements to an array, use this method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to avoid multiple reallocations. This method ensures that the array has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unique, mutable, contiguous storage, with space allocated for at least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the requested number of elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For performance reasons, the size of the newly allocated storage might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greater than the requested capacity. Use the array’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to determine the size of the new storage."}]},{"anchor":"Preserving-an-Arrays-Geometric-Growth-Strategy","type":"heading","level":1,"text":"Preserving an Array’s Geometric Growth Strategy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you implement a custom data structure backed by an array that grows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamically, naively calling the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method can lead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to worse than expected performance. Arrays need to follow a geometric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation pattern for appending elements to achieve amortized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant-time performance. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" type’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":" methods take care of this detail for you, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" allocates only as much space as you tell it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(padded to a round value), and no more. This avoids over-allocation, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can result in insertion not having amortized constant-time performance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following code declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":", an array of integers, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"type":"text","text":" function, which adds ten more values to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array on each call."}]},{"code":["  var values: [Int] = [0, 1, 2, 3]","","  \/\/ Don't use 'reserveCapacity(_:)' like this","  func addTenQuadratic() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      values.reserveCapacity(newCount)","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" increases the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" array’s capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by exactly 10 elements on each pass through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is linear growth. Instead of having constant time when averaged over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many calls, the function may decay to performance that is linear in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values.count"},{"type":"text","text":". This is almost certainly not what you want."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases like this, the simplest fix is often to simply remove the call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and let the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method grow the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for you."}]},{"code":["  func addTen() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need more control over the capacity of your array, implement your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own geometric growth strategy, passing the size you compute to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is the number of elements in the array.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/contiguousarray\/reservecapacity(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ContiguousArray"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"Swift","externalID":"s:s15ContiguousArrayV15reserveCapacityyySiF","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"reserveCapacity(_:)","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"macOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"tvOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"visionOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/ContiguousArray/reserveCapacity(_:)":{"type":"topic","title":"reserveCapacity(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ContiguousArray\/reserveCapacity(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/contiguousarray\/reservecapacity(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Int":{"title":"Int","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/int","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Int"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","abstract":[{"text":"A signed integer value type.","type":"text"}]},"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}],"alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background.","type":"image","identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","title":"Swift","kind":"symbol","images":[{"identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","type":"card"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/ContiguousArray":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContiguousArray"}],"title":"ContiguousArray","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContiguousArray"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ContiguousArray","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/contiguousarray","abstract":[{"text":"A contiguously stored array.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"}}}